@smarterclayton I pushed an update to the test because the new server fixture wasn't working for some reason. I instead updated the existing fixture and other tests in the file to use the smaller model, which makes them all run faster too (by the way, `--enforce-eager` makes server startup time quicker).

However, the new test adds quite a lot of time .. with the model change the file takes 1:52 to run without the new test and 3:52 to run with it (this is actually with one of the 6 subtests commented out). I think mainly because each of the different `--host` variations means another server launch.  There might not be much of a way around that though until we make more improvements to the startup time (we have a current focus on this and also on shortening CI time).

Also the `localhost` variant fails for me locally, will see if it also fails in the CI and if so I guess we could exclude that one.

```suggestion
    if host and is_valid_ipv6_address(host):
```

```suggestion
    elif host and is_valid_ipv4_address(host):
```

